                                "sense_id": "56592d44-75ee-367c-9a73-9965b0236d42",
                                "text": "When we arrived at one of those soda ponds, being a little backwash slough with a white deposit over the top, I collected a pocketful of dust that goes by the western name of “saleratus,” which is practically the identical same thing as baking soda, and really first-rate for undigestion."
